{
    "id": "lesson-fables-personification-02",
    "title": "Personification — Giving Life to Fable Creatures & Nature",
    "description": "Learn what Personification is and how writers use it to give human actions, emotions, and speech to animals, objects, and forces of nature — and discover why this technique is what makes fable characters and settings feel so vividly alive.",
    "author": "AST English Curriculum Team",
    "level": "Year 4 (Intermediate)",
    "duration": 30,
    "createdAt": "2026-08-09T06:39:00.000Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-08-09T06:39:00.000Z",
    "settings": {
        "theme": "dark-cinematic",
        "subject": "English Language",
        "module": "Fables & Figurative Language"
    },
    "slides": [
        {
            "id": "slide-p-01",
            "title": "What is Personification?",
            "status": "uncompleted",
            "state": "active",
            "components": [
                {
                    "id": "heading-p-1",
                    "type": "heading",
                    "props": {
                        "content": "Bringing the World to Life: Personification",
                        "level": 1,
                        "align": "left"
                    },
                    "state": "active",
                    "status": "uncompleted"
                },
                {
                    "id": "paragraph-p-1",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "props": {
                        "content": "<strong>Personification</strong> is a figurative language technique where a writer gives <em>human qualities</em> — such as actions, emotions, or speech — to animals, objects, or forces of nature that cannot actually think or feel.",
                        "align": "left"
                    },
                    "state": "active",
                    "status": "uncompleted"
                },
                {
                    "id": "image-p-1",
                    "type": "image",
                    "props": {
                        "src": "/placeholder.svg?height=300&width=640",
                        "alt": "A smiling golden sun with arms stretching over a green meadow, while a cloud weeps rain tears",
                        "caption": "When the sun smiles and a cloud cries, we are giving them human emotions — that is Personification!",
                        "width": "100%"
                    },
                    "state": "active",
                    "status": "uncompleted"
                },
                {
                    "id": "paragraph-p-2",
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "props": {
                        "content": "Think of it this way: the sun cannot actually smile, the wind cannot actually whisper, and a tree cannot actually wave hello. But when a writer says they can, the world suddenly feels <strong>alive and magical</strong>.",
                        "align": "left"
                    },
                    "state": "active",
                    "status": "uncompleted"
                },
                {
                    "id": "flashcards-p-1",
                    "type": "flashcards",
                    "props": {
                        "title": "Personification Quick Discovery Cards",
                        "mode": "practice",
                        "cards": [
                            {
                                "id": "fc-p-1",
                                "front": "The hungry river swallowed the fallen leaves.",
                                "back": "PERSONIFICATION! 'Hungry' and 'swallowed' are human actions given to a river. Rivers cannot feel hunger or eat."
                            },
                            {
                                "id": "fc-p-2",
                                "front": "The wind screamed through the narrow mountain pass.",
                                "back": "PERSONIFICATION! 'Screamed' is a human action. Wind makes sound but cannot scream with emotion."
                            },
                            {
                                "id": "fc-p-3",
                                "front": "The oak tree bowed its ancient head in greeting.",
                                "back": "PERSONIFICATION! 'Bowed' and 'greeting' are human social actions given to a tree. Trees bend in wind but cannot bow in respect."
                            },
                            {
                                "id": "fc-p-4",
                                "front": "The river is approximately 400 metres wide.",
                                "back": "NOT personification. This is a plain, literal statement of fact — no human qualities are given to the river."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "state": "active",
                    "status": "uncompleted",
                    "mode": "practice"
                },
                {
                    "id": "quiz-p-1",
                    "type": "quiz",
                    "props": {
                        "mode": "practice",
                        "points": 10,
                        "showExplanation": true,
                        "shuffleOptions": true,
                        "randomizeAnswers": true,
                        "questions": [
                            {
                                "id": "q-p-1",
                                "question": "Which of the following is the most accurate definition of Personification?",
                                "options": [
                                    {
                                        "id": "qp1-a",
                                        "text": "Comparing two things using the words 'like' or 'as'",
                                        "isCorrect": false
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "id": "qp1-b",
                                        "text": "Giving human qualities (actions, emotions, speech) to non-human things",
                                        "isCorrect": true
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "id": "qp1-c",
                                        "text": "Saying one thing is exactly the same as another thing",
                                        "isCorrect": false
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "id": "qp1-d",
                                        "text": "Repeating the same first letter in a sentence",
                                        "isCorrect": false
                                    }
                                ],
                                "explanation": "Personification = giving human behaviour, emotions, or speech to animals, objects, or nature. Not comparisons (that is Similes) or direct equivalences (that is Metaphors)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "state": "active",
                    "status": "uncompleted",
                    "mode": "practice"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
